# Testing

Visual checks are slow. Do not inspect how the page looks unless the user explicitly asks.

- Do not take screenshots, record the screen, compare layouts, or review pixels, spacing, colors, or viewports.
- Do not produce walkthrough artifacts, demo videos, or cropped frames to judge appearance.
- Do verify the behavior you changed. Load the page, click and type through that flow, and assert the resulting state: text, attributes, dialogs, and stored values.
- Fail the check if the browser console reports an error or an uncaught exception.
- A headless script that drives the page is enough. Desktop and mobile visual passes are out of scope.
- The offline reload check is the same kind of check: install the worker, disable the network, reload, and assert that the page still responds and the console stays clean.
